s 93 passed.\n\nChanges:\n- **`llm/logs.py`**: added `_output_segment_hashes` and the `_output_message_hashes` row key. `log_row_extras` now finds tool calls and server results in the turn's output messages, marks each call and result with `server_executed`, and takes result ids from the matching message set.\n- **`llm/cli.py`**: `_output_message_hashes` is stripped from output. The per-result printing moved into a nested `_display_tool_results` helper. Local results keep their place in the prompt section, and server results print under `### Tool results` after `### Tool calls`.\n- **`docs/changelog.md`**: added the bullet under Unreleased.\n\nDeviation from the spec: in `cli.py` I read the flag with `tool_result.get(\"server_executed\")` instead of `tool_result[\"server_executed\"]`. Legacy rows build `tool_results` from a JSON SQL blob without that key, so the plain lookup would raise `KeyError` on old responses. The spec's \"(no `server_executed`)\" wording allows this.\n\nNot run: ruff isn't installed in `.venv`, so I skipped lint and format checks. I didn't run the full test suite, only the two files the spec lists. I didn't commit; `SPEC.md` is still untracked.", "ttft_ms": 2101, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 57075, "uuid": "64e44605-84ae-49cc-b54a-287be7cdbe13", "ttft_stream_ms": 1768, "time_to_request_ms": 430, "first_content_frame_ms": 1768, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
